# Best Practices

This guide provides recommendations to help sellers create high-quality products and build a successful presence on the Codexeron Marketplace.

Following these best practices can improve customer satisfaction, increase product visibility, and support long-term success.

---

# Build Quality Products

High-quality products create better customer experiences.

Before publishing your product:

- Test all features.
- Remove unnecessary files.
- Fix known issues.
- Ensure stable performance.
- Verify compatibility.

Quality products receive better feedback and require less support.

---

# Write Clear Documentation

Every product should include complete and easy-to-follow documentation.

Documentation should explain:

- Installation
- Configuration
- Requirements
- Features
- Troubleshooting
- Update instructions

Well-written documentation reduces customer questions and support requests.

---

# Keep Products Updated

Regular updates demonstrate ongoing maintenance.

Consider updating your product to:

- Fix bugs
- Improve performance
- Add new features
- Improve compatibility
- Enhance security

Always include a changelog with every release.

---

# Provide Accurate Information

Your product page should accurately describe your product.

Include:

- Clear descriptions
- Real screenshots
- Supported versions
- System requirements
- License information

Do not exaggerate features or functionality.

---

# Support Your Customers

Providing helpful support builds trust.

Good support includes:

- Responding politely
- Answering questions clearly
- Fixing confirmed issues
- Updating documentation when needed

Professional communication improves customer satisfaction.

---

# Follow Marketplace Policies

Every seller is expected to follow Codexeron Marketplace policies.

This includes respecting:

- Copyright
- Licensing
- Security standards
- Marketplace rules

Policy violations may result in product rejection or account restrictions.

---

# Improve Continuously

Successful sellers regularly review customer feedback.

Use feedback to:

- Improve usability
- Fix reported issues
- Add requested features
- Enhance documentation

Continuous improvement increases long-term product value.

---

# Security Recommendations

Always prioritize security.

- Protect customer data.
- Validate user input.
- Keep dependencies updated.
- Avoid exposing sensitive information.
- Follow secure coding practices.

Security is an essential part of product quality.

---

# Professionalism

Maintain a professional presence by:

- Using clear product names
- Writing accurate descriptions
- Keeping your profile up to date
- Delivering consistent quality
- Treating customers respectfully

Professional sellers build long-term trust.

